// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: rm -rf %t.d
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/runner-scenarios.py start-fail --only missing,ends --work %t.d --programs %S/Inputs/runner
// SPLIT: runner-failures 1/4
// P04.19 (D4.14): failures that are not the program's own. An executor that
// does not start (no such program, one that ends at once, one that never says
// it is ready) gives every program the same `internal` result in bounded time
// (after three failed starts in a row no more are tried) and `gopp test-run`
// exits 1; a JIT link error (undefined C functions, named in sorted order) and
// a compile error are results of their program, and the others still run, on
// the same executor.
